{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "bijective x^3:\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  x^3 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)\n  surjective onto the reals: yes\n  proved: a polynomial of odd degree 3 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)\n  bijective: yes\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "bijective", "ucas": "bijective x^3", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "bijective", "injective": "yes (one-to-one)", "surjective_onto_the_reals": "yes", "proved": "a polynomial of odd degree 3 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)", "bijective": "yes", "headline": "bijective x^3:", "details": ["x^3 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "bijective x^3:\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  x^3 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)\n  surjective onto the reals: yes\n  proved: a polynomial of odd degree 3 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)\n  bijective: yes\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "bijective x^2:\n  injective: no\n  witness: f(-1) = f(1) = 1 with x = -1 and x = 1\n  the value is taken on two pieces of monotonicity (pieces proved, witness solved by bisection)\n  surjective onto the reals: no\n  witness: -1 is never taken\n  f is bounded below by 0: proved: an even-degree polynomial with a positive leading coefficient has a minimum, 0 at x = 0 (a root of f')\n  bijective: no\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "bijective", "ucas": "bijective x^2", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "bijective", "injective": "no", "witness": ["f(-1) = f(1) = 1 with x = -1 and x = 1", "-1 is never taken"], "surjective_onto_the_reals": "no", "f_is_bounded_below_by_0": "proved: an even-degree polynomial with a positive leading coefficient has a minimum, 0 at x = 0 (a root of f')", "bijective": "no", "headline": "bijective x^2:", "details": ["the value is taken on two pieces of monotonicity (pieces proved, witness solved by bisection)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "bijective x^2:\n  injective: no\n  witness: f(-1) = f(1) = 1 with x = -1 and x = 1\n  the value is taken on two pieces of monotonicity (pieces proved, witness solved by bisection)\n  surjective onto the reals: no\n  witness: -1 is never taken\n  f is bounded below by 0: proved: an even-degree polynomial with a positive leading coefficient has a minimum, 0 at x = 0 (a root of f')\n  bijective: no\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "bijective exp(x):\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  exp(x) is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (checked numerically)\n  surjective onto the reals: no\n  witness: -1 is never taken\n  f is bounded below by 4.539992976e-05: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0; the smallest value seen is 4.539992976e-05 at x = -10\n  bijective: no\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "bijective", "ucas": "bijective exp(x)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "bijective", "injective": "yes (one-to-one)", "surjective_onto_the_reals": "no", "witness": "-1 is never taken", "f_is_bounded_below_by_4_539992976e_05": "proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0; the smallest value seen is 4.539992976e-05 at x = -10", "bijective": "no", "headline": "bijective exp(x):", "details": ["exp(x) is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (checked numerically)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "bijective exp(x):\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  exp(x) is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (checked numerically)\n  surjective onto the reals: no\n  witness: -1 is never taken\n  f is bounded below by 4.539992976e-05: proved by interval arithmetic: f >= 0; the smallest value seen is 4.539992976e-05 at x = -10\n  bijective: no\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "bijective 2x + 1:\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  2x + 1 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)\n  surjective onto the reals: yes\n  proved: a polynomial of odd degree 1 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)\n  bijective: yes\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "bijective", "ucas": "bijective 2*x+1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "bijective", "injective": "yes (one-to-one)", "surjective_onto_the_reals": "yes", "proved": "a polynomial of odd degree 1 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)", "bijective": "yes", "headline": "bijective 2x + 1:", "details": ["2x + 1 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "bijective 2x + 1:\n  injective: yes (one-to-one)\n  2x + 1 is strictly increasing, so no two inputs share a value (proved)\n  surjective onto the reals: yes\n  proved: a polynomial of odd degree 1 is continuous and tends to -inf and +inf, so it takes every value (intermediate value theorem)\n  bijective: yes\n"}, "isError": false}}
